<% content_for :title, "Replica demo" %>
<style>
  /* home.scss sets every div to 100px by 100px. Reset that for this page. */
  .demo,
  .demo div,
  .demo section,
  .demo form,
  .demo ul,
  .demo li,
  .demo pre,
  .demo p,
  .demo h1,
  .demo h2 {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    min-height: 0;
    margin: 0;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .demo {
    width: min(46rem, calc(100% - 2rem));
    margin: 2rem auto 3rem;
    padding: 0 0.25rem;
    font: 17px/1.55 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    color: #1c1c1c;
  }
  .demo h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .demo h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1.4rem 0 0.45rem; }
  .demo p { margin: 0.6rem 0; }
  .demo section { margin: 1.1rem 0; }
  .demo .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem; align-items: center; }
  .demo .actions a,
  .demo .actions button {
    font: inherit;
    line-height: 1.3;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid #b9b9b9;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: #fff;
    color: #14315c;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .demo .result,
  .demo pre {
    background: #f4f4f4;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .demo .bad { background: #fde8e8; }
  .demo pre { white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
  .demo ul { margin: 0.3rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .demo li { margin: 0.3rem 0; }
</style>

<div class="demo">
  <h1>Replica demo</h1>
  <p>
    Same split as tac_webschool. <code>:writing</code> is the primary.
    <code>:reading</code> is the replica (<code>replica: true</code> in <code>database.yml</code>).
    This page does what a 成績表 GET does: it reads, then it writes.
    DatabaseSelector is still off. The primary adapter is now
    <code>postgresql_proxy</code>, with <code>proxy_delay</code> 0.
  </p>

  <section>
    <div class="actions">
      <%= link_to "Selector off", replica_demo_path(mode: "off") %>
      <%= link_to "DatabaseSelector GET", replica_demo_path(mode: "selector") %>
      <%= button_to "POST, then selector GET", replica_demo_path, method: :post %>
      <%= link_to "Read on replica, write on primary", replica_demo_path(mode: "split") %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="<%= @error ? "result bad" : "result" %>">
    <% if @mode == "off" %>
      <p>Nothing wrapped this GET. That is the tac_webschool case: DatabaseSelector is off, and the action is not wrapped one block at a time. The proxy sent the count to <code>:reading</code> and the insert to <code>:writing</code>. The hit was saved. <code>proxy_delay</code> 0 means a write does not hold the next SELECT on the primary.</p>
    <% elsif @mode == "selector" %>
      <% if @selector_role == :writing %>
        <p>The POST button stamped <code>session[:last_write]</code> <%= number_with_precision(@last_write_age, precision: 1) %>s ago. tac_webschool does not stamp that key. This page then wrapped the GET as <code>:writing</code> with <code>prevent_writes</code> true, which is what DatabaseSelector does inside its 2 second window. That wrap stays on the proxy. <code>proxy_delay</code> 0 still sent the count to <code>:reading</code>. The insert went to <code>:writing</code> and was saved, because the proxy opens its own writing connection and that connection does not keep the outer <code>prevent_writes</code>.</p>
      <% else %>
        <p>No recent non-GET, so this page wrapped the GET as <code>:reading</code> with <code>prevent_writes</code> true. That wrap leaves the proxy and uses the replica adapter. The count ran there. The insert was refused. The first button stays on the proxy, and that one does save.</p>
      <% end %>
      <% if @error %>
        <p><strong>ReadOnlyError.</strong> <%= @error.message %></p>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <p>This button still wraps the count and the insert by hand. The proxy already does that split for the first button, without a wrap. An explicit <code>connected_to</code> still wins over the proxy.</p>
    <% end %>
    <p>Rows visible to the read: <%= @read_count %>. <%= @saved ? "Saved hit #{@saved.id}." : "No hit saved." %></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>SQL in this request</h2>
    <pre id="sql"><%= @sql.join("\n") %></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Recent hits</h2>
    <ul>
      <% @hits.each do |hit| %>
        <li><%= hit.verb %> — <%= hit.note %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>